  "answer": "The assistant should answer that the sales note’s claim of “immediate deletion on request” is not the binding policy. Under the official Security and Data Governance Policy, standard deletion occurs within 90 days after contract termination: the workspace is suspended for 30 days, active databases and indexes are purged by day 60, and backup/cold storage cryptographic erasure is completed within 120 days of contract termination [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. While data is immediately removed from active user access and TutorChat queries, physical deletion from primary storage and backups takes up to 90 days [NL-019#NL-019-S05]. Sales claims that conflict with this policy are informal and do not supersede it [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. Custom deletion timelines can be negotiated for Enterprise customers, but they must be documented in a signed DPA and configured by engineering [NL-007#NL-007-S06]. The sales playbook also instructs reps not to promise immediate deletion without consulting the Security and Governance Lead and to follow the official 90-day standard [NL-009#NL-009-S08]. Therefore, the sales note should be corrected: immediate deletion is not standard unless a custom DPA expressly provides otherwise.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
